	(text "Coil: tools/coil_gen.py, about 6.6 uH. Untuned it lands near 14.06 MHz with the 18.4 pF\ntag input, so C1 trims it down to 13.56 MHz. Fit C1 after lamination, never before:\nthe skin and epoxy pull the resonance down too."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21cc88aa-754b-4c55-bad8-dc0426cce4c3")
	)
	(text "C3-C5 are the fade bank. They also set the in-rush: InRushTarget must charge them before\nthe MCU browns out. C5 is DNP until I've measured the fade on prototype 1.\nTag VCC sags through 1.55-1.62 V during the fade, which the datasheet says to avoid. The\nfield is gone by then, so a tag reset there is harmless."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "954cde37-bd55-4cde-8159-cf64b0361930")
	)
	(text "VCC absolute max is 2.0 V, so the whole board runs on the 1.8 V harvest output (GPIO1\nin down-stream power mode, DefaultTarget 0x0x). The reader has to send ManageGPIO SET to\nturn it on; a plain NDEF read never does, so LEDs only light from the app.\nBackpower (GPIO1Config bit 0) must be set so the tag can keep talking during harvesting."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f1e03cd3-57fa-4275-b692-db52270ae4d8")
	)
